Quoting Allan Joergensen:

>>   Replies to the List-Post address
> Outlook and Thunderbird does not have this functionality.

No, but if hit "reply all" in thunderbird (as you usually would do on
mailing lists), the reply will go to the Mail-Followup-To: address
(which you have set). And there's a TB extension for using List-Post.
There are still MUAs not using Mail-Followup-To, so I let my MTA also
set Reply-To to the list address.

Leaving the technical discussion, I'd say that on a list where you
usually have experienced users (like the ones on this list should be),
no reply-to munging should be done. On some non-IT-topic, I would
probably do it.


